{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788491289225699001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"princely-courageous-milksnake","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6917c8f7a71daf17e07ed4df9eaf75d0497f87f15d03a760fd17c153fabaffe5","event_uuid":"f6679091-b9e8-4f3f-9e1f-eb69f21d4816","position":{"commit_sha":"5d15669dec51351fa3fcc59626cd5a0b46c7c604","position":"1788481636576004001-f6679091-b9e8-4f3f-9e1f-eb69f21d4816"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"febfdce4a37ff13a669d0a695f44d0145ba39738594302eb6977f2c949756656","event_uuid":"e686c052-1128-4dc1-8f04-3cfb174365a7","position":{"commit_sha":"a6a664f2f626587b3dd1affa592294c8897d945f","position":"1788481682475959001-e686c052-1128-4dc1-8f04-3cfb174365a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7f1745caf8d12dcc03856a394805779c4937fafd429dadc5dc0eb0793a16a81b","event_uuid":"b70d6cce-7af6-482f-a5d8-45be5cb8672f","position":{"commit_sha":"076435edf01a0caf1d837e3debdf45987587bbdc","position":"1788481821802713001-b70d6cce-7af6-482f-a5d8-45be5cb8672f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f26270c55b865fe640bed1e166f33e52f9b9b57cfd20b69dab25666b55cbbc84","event_uuid":"a31c8d9f-cdca-4fbd-bae3-ae1a1ee8532f","position":{"commit_sha":"de7769cc3a6f437da093e534f3597de6de20f3c0","position":"1788489316259929001-a31c8d9f-cdca-4fbd-bae3-ae1a1ee8532f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DIRECTION FROM OPERATOR: do not pin a local update tool. Recording the consequences, and a correction to my own earlier recommendation.\n\nMY RECOMMENDATION WAS WRONG ON THE FACTS. I proposed 'brew upgrade uv' as the minimal unblock. That cannot work: required-version is '==0.12.7', an EXACT pin, and Homebrew has moved PAST it to 0.12.9 (2026-09-01). Verified empirically against a scratch pyproject carrying the same pin:\n  /opt/homebrew/bin/uv 0.12.9  -> error: Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.12.9`\n  ~/.local/bin/uv     0.12.7  -> Resolved 1 package\nUpgrading Homebrew only changes which number appears in the error. The scheduled 00:32 run confirms it independently: it failed with 0.12.9 and pushed the streak to 120. I should have checked the pin's comparison operator before recommending an upgrade.\n\nTHIS IS THE FEBD FAILURE, VERSION FOR VERSION. scripts/check_uv_pin.py's docstring describes the outage as: 'every build died with Required uv version ==0.12.7 does not match the running version 0.12.9 the moment :latest moved -- a time bomb armed by an upstream release, with no change to this repository.' The version in that sentence is 0.12.9, which is what Homebrew now ships. So this host's updater is the SAME time bomb with a different fuse: not a floating Docker tag, but a package manager that upgraded past the pin. Four consumers of one exact pin, three of which were never brought along.\n\nRELAXING THE PIN IS NOT AVAILABLE. check_uv_pin.py deliberately fails the build when the pin is 'loosened to a range' (its point 2) or overridden per call site (point 3), because an exact pin is the property under test. So the fix cannot be a wider constraint in pyproject.toml.\n\nWHAT THE DIRECTION MEANS FOR AC2. The updater is a local dev-tracking tool, not CI; it gains no reproducibility from being locked to any particular uv binary, and the current hardcode (UV_BIN default /opt/homebrew/bin/uv at rebar-dev-update.sh:18) is itself a local pin -- the one that broke. So AC2 stands as written and should be read as explicitly EXCLUDING a new hardcoded path: the updater must DERIVE the uv it needs from the CANDIDATE COMMIT's own required-version at sync time, since that value changes as main moves, and fail loudly naming required version, found version, and paths inspected when none satisfies it. Substituting one absolute path for another (either direction) is rejected -- it re-inverts the moment the other side updates first, which is exactly how this stall was born.\n\nAC3 RESCOPED per operator decision: do NOT pursue the cross-account SNS authorization. The alert sink stays as-is. AC4 (a LOCAL detector that surfaces a stalled updater or an over-stale build without depending on the remote sink) absorbs the detection requirement and is the priority half -- it is the thing that would actually have caught 120 silent failures.\n\nIMMEDIATE STATE: no persistent host change made. No plist edit, no REBAR_DEV_UV_BIN pin. Homebrew's uv did move 0.12.6 -> 0.12.9 during investigation (a relink surfaced by 'brew upgrade'; both versions fail the pin identically, so no behavior changed). The global rebar remains at cdfd7d94d and stale until AC2 lands or an operator runs a one-shot.","timestamp":1788489316259929001}],"created_at":1788481636576004001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e686c052-1128-4dc1-8f04-3cfb174365a7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"},{"link_uuid":"b70d6cce-7af6-482f-a5d8-45be5cb8672f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"febd-6b13-1976-43be"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nThe hourly LaunchAgent `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`, which keeps this host's **global**\n`rebar` / `rebar-mcp` aligned to `origin/main`, has failed **119 consecutive times**. The global\nbuild is pinned at `cdfd7d94dc2fe7671a7eba48e31f36c30f39235c` (2026-08-28) — roughly **195 commits\nbehind** `origin/main` and about five days stale. `launchctl list` reports last exit status **1**\nfor the agent (the sibling `rebar-worktree-gc` and `rebar-serena-mirror-update` agents report 0).\n\nEvery hourly run logs the same rejection:\n\n```\n2026-09-03T23:29:51Z start (installed-good=cdfd7d94d... remote-main=ebbcd7a030d6...)\nerror: Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.12.6`\n2026-09-03T23:32:05Z candidate ebbcd7a030d6... rejected at sync; current left untouched\n2026-09-03T23:32:06Z candidate-rejection streak now 119 (latest stage: sync)\n```\n\n118 of the 119 rejections are this uv mismatch; one is an unrelated transient\n(`fetch-pack: unexpected disconnect ... early EOF`, rejected at the `checkout` stage).\n\n## Root cause: an inverted assumption, not a missing upgrade\n\n`~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh:18` hardcodes the uv binary:\n\n```sh\nUV_BIN=\"${REBAR_DEV_UV_BIN:-/opt/homebrew/bin/uv}\"\n```\n\nand `:120` deliberately orders PATH to keep that binary authoritative, with the reasoning stated\nat `:116-118`:\n\n```sh\n# launchd gives a minimal PATH. Keep Homebrew before ~/.local/bin so the obsolete\n# standalone uv there cannot shadow the pinned UV_BIN.\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/bin:${HOME}/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin\"\n```\n\nMeasured on this host:\n\n| binary | version | date |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv` | **0.12.6** | Homebrew, 2026-08-25 |\n| `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/uv` | **0.12.7** | standalone, 2026-08-27 |\n\nThe repo pins `required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` in `pyproject.toml:346` (landed in commit\n`7501cc1d602d`, \"Pin uv once so CI stops resolving it remotely\"). uv reads `required-version`\nitself and fails fast, so `:344`'s `\"$UV_BIN\" sync` aborts every run.\n\n**The comment's premise has inverted.** When it was written the `~/.local/bin` standalone was the\nobsolete one, so pinning to Homebrew was right. Homebrew is now the stale side. The guard written\nto prevent a stale uv from being selected is now the mechanism selecting a stale uv. Hardcoding\neither absolute path just re-inverts the next time one side updates first.\n\n## This is the same pin that caused a production outage\n\n`required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` also broke the on-box container builds when their Dockerfiles used\na floating `uv:latest` tag — the root cause of the multi-hour MCP outage tracked under bug `febd`.\nThat fix pinned `infra/compose/Dockerfile.{mcp,reviewbot,opcert}` to `uv:0.12.7` and extended\n`scripts/check_uv_pin.py` to scan Dockerfiles. **This host's updater is a third consumer of the same\npin that was never brought along**, and it is outside `check_uv_pin.py`'s reach because it is a\nmachine-local script, not a tracked repo file.\n\n## The alert built to catch exactly this cannot deliver\n\n`docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md` documents a `REJECT_STREAK_ALERT` (default **3**) added\nafter a prior incident it describes as: *\"the b477339a99 incident: 43 hourly `sync` rejections,\n~48 commits behind, no signal\"*. The alert is firing correctly and failing to deliver on every\nattempt:\n\n```\naws: [ERROR]: An error occurred (AuthorizationError) when calling the Publish operation:\nUser: arn:aws:iam::820258254566:user/joeoakhart is not authorized to perform: SNS:Publish\non resource: arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:896586841071:rebar-gerrit-alerts\nbecause no resource-based policy allows the SNS:Publish action\nERROR: aws sns publish failed for alert 'reject-streak'\n```\n\nThe IAM principal is in account **820258254566**; the SNS topic is in account **896586841071**.\nNo resource-based policy on the topic permits the cross-account publish. So the streak reached\n**119 against a threshold of 3** with zero operator signal — a strictly worse recurrence of the\nvery incident the alert was introduced to prevent. **The detection gap is the more important half\nof this bug: without it, the next stall is equally silent regardless of what caused it.**\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery agent session on this host that invokes the global `rebar` has, for about five days, been\nrunning a build ~195 commits stale. The gate's own advisory says it plainly:\n\n> \"this rebar build (cdfd7d94d, 2026-08-29, dirty) is 195 commit(s) BEHIND the ref this gate\n> pinned (08a39c39c) — it may predate recent config keys and gate fixes, so **results can be wrong\n> in ways the verdict cannot show**.\"\n\nThat reaches plan-review and completion-verifier verdicts produced through the global tool, not\njust this session's. This was noticed only because a subagent's gate log was read closely.\n\n## Secondary defect observed\n\n`~/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.err.log` shows the pruner failing to reclaim release dirs:\n\n```\nrm: .../releases/5b5008bbfbec...66068/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages: Directory not empty\nrm: .../releases/5fb693345b0c...1559: Directory not empty\n```\n\n`releases/5fb693345b0cd1b48d1e9d20b292fd15761c7624.1559` is a 3-entry stub — a partially built\nrelease that was never completed or cleaned. Related to the disk-ceiling work under epic\n`6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`, since these release dirs are ~346 MB each.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAll deterministic and verifiable in a single run — no waiting for the hourly timer or for a\nrecurrence.\n\n1. Running the updater on demand\n   (`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`) publishes a `current`\n   whose `sha` equals `origin/main` at that moment, and appends no `Required uv version` error to\n   `update.log`. `reject-streak` returns to 0.\n2. The updater selects a uv that **satisfies the repo's declared `required-version`**, rather than\n   hardcoding an absolute path to either candidate. It must not be re-broken by whichever of\n   Homebrew / standalone updates first next time. If no available uv satisfies the pin, the run\n   must fail with a message naming the required version, the version found, and the paths\n   inspected — never a bare mismatch line.\n   Verify by pointing the resolver at a deliberately wrong uv and observing that message.\n3. The reject-streak alert reaches the operator. Either the cross-account SNS publish is\n   authorized, or the sink is changed to one this host's IAM principal can actually write.\n   Verified by forcing an alert (e.g. `REBAR_DEV_ALERT_CMD` or a threshold override) and observing\n   delivery — not by waiting for the next real stall.\n4. A stalled updater is detectable **locally**, without depending on the alert path at all — for\n   example a `rebar` invocation surfacing that the running build is more than N commits behind, or\n   a check script an operator can run. Rationale: this stall persisted 119 hours because the only\n   detector was a remote sink that silently 403'd.\n5. The pruner's `Directory not empty` failures are resolved, and the partial release stub\n   `5fb693345b0cd...1559` is reclaimed.\n\n## Notes for whoever takes this\n\n- `rebar-dev-update.sh` already honours a `REBAR_DEV_UV_BIN` override, so a fix can be staged\n  without editing the script if needed for an immediate unblock.\n- The script is **machine-local** and git-ignored, so a repo-side test cannot cover it directly.\n  Consider whether `scripts/check_uv_pin.py` should grow an operator-runnable mode that checks\n  local consumers of the pin, which would satisfy AC4's spirit and stay portable (no CI provider\n  dependency).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"],["relates_to","febd-6b13-1976-43be"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["bug","ops","tooling","local-env","alerting"],"ticket_id":"ae97-a37b-9fa3-413a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Hourly rebar-dev updater stalled 119 runs on a uv version mismatch; global rebar is ~195 commits stale and the reject-streak alert cannot deliver (cross-account SNS 403)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f6679091-b9e8-4f3f-9e1f-eb69f21d4816","e686c052-1128-4dc1-8f04-3cfb174365a7","b70d6cce-7af6-482f-a5d8-45be5cb8672f","a31c8d9f-cdca-4fbd-bae3-ae1a1ee8532f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788491289225699001,"uuid":"86a9f8aa-fddc-47eb-857c-988e42c5eebe"}